Background (already diagnosed, trust this): /dayjs/src/plugin/weekYear/index.js currently reads:
```js
export default (o, c) => {
  const proto = c.prototype
  proto.weekYear = function () {
    const month = this.month()
    const weekOfYear = this.week()
    const year = this.year()
    if (weekOfYear === 1 && month === 11) {
      return year + 1
    }
    return year
  }
}
```
It only handles the December/week-1 case. The symmetric case is missing: a January date whose week() is 52 or 53 belongs to the PREVIOUS week-year (e.g. with a locale having weekStart: 1, yearStart: 4, `dayjs('2021-01-01').week()` is 53 but `weekYear()` wrongly returns 2021 instead of 2020; moment returns 2020). The docs at /dayjs/docs/en/I18n.md document `yearStart: 4` ("the week that contains Jan 4th is the first week of the year"), and /dayjs/test/plugin/weekYear.test.js compares against moment.

REQUIRED FIX (edit only /dayjs/src/plugin/weekYear/index.js): add the missing branch so the function becomes:
```js
export default (o, c) => {
  const proto = c.prototype
  proto.weekYear = function () {
    const month = this.month()
    const weekOfYear = this.week()
    const year = this.year()
    if (weekOfYear === 1 && month === 11) {
      return year + 1
    }
    if (month === 0 && weekOfYear >= 52) {
      return year - 1
    }
    return year
  }
}
```

